use wheel gui_input to adjust zoom. Ensure the world scene connects minimap_objects \\\"removed\\\" signals to the minimap while mobs/crates have the \\\"removed\\\" signals, expose each one's \\\"minimap_icon\\\", and ensure mobs/crates belong to the minimap_objects group.\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/task_config.json","text":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Implement the minimap logic: export a Player reference and a zoom property with a clamped setter, cache the grid and marker prototypes, center the player marker after the first frame, compute grid_scale from the grid size and viewport, duplicate and show markers for every node in the minimap_objects group using their minimap_icon keys, store them in a 'markers' dictionary, rotate (player rotation + PI/2) and position markers each frame relative to the player (scaling to 0.75 and clamping when off the grid), implement _on_object_removed which removes and erases markers when called, and implement _on_gui_input which handles mouse wheel gui_input to adjust zoom. Ensure the world scene connects minimap_objects \\\"removed\\\" signals to the minimap while mobs/crates have the \\\"removed\\\" signals, expose each one's \\\"minimap_icon\\\", and ensure mobs/crates belong to the minimap_objects group.\"\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":3,"totalLines":3,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/task_config.json","time":{"start":1790387298239,"end":1790387298262}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_029e038577869470016ab72460ec508196b568244164d150af"}},"id":"prt_0db661fbc001JNP6BOHyA5zOB4","sessionID":"ses_f249c6d95ffeOdW8h0CK3lJyRA","messageID":"msg_0db6584e8001kthTqvVQyR0Rw4"}}
